  "summary": "Split the largest Settings markup, run-monitor JavaScript, and Settings builder styles into bounded WebView-owned modules without changing backend routes, persistence, lifecycle, media policy, DOM contracts, accessibility, keyboard behavior, or public exports.",
  "reason": "The three parent assets are large context and coupling hotspots (2,304-line Settings partial, 1,849-line run-monitor view, and 2,206-line Settings builder stylesheet). Domain/component slices reduce maintenance and retrieval cost while retaining the existing no-build WebView architecture.",
